<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mularaja II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1175–1178</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mularaja">Mularaja</a> II was a child king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaulukya-dynasty">Chaulukya dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, ruling from about 1175 to 1178 under the regency of his mother Naikidevi. In 1178 the Chaulukya army defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-of-ghor">Muhammad of Ghor</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kasahrada">Battle of Kasahrada</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-abu">Mount Abu</a>, one of the few defeats suffered by the Ghurid ruler in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p></div>
